<title>FRANCE: Rhone-Poulenc wants to cut pay-out ratio.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc wants to cut pay-out ratio.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc plans to reduce its dividend pay-out ratio to 35-40 percent from 41 percent in 1996, finance director Jean-Pierre Tirouflet said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The pay-out ratio has fallen from 45 to 41 percent. Our objective is to bring it down to 35 to 40 percent which is more comparable with what happens elsewhere and with our equity and debt situation,&quot; he told the annual general meeting.</p>
</text>
